@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the one list of PROVEO_* variables proveo's Go reads or sets — who sets each, what it defaults to, how `proveo help env` shows it, and the two tests that keep the list and the code equal
' covers: internal/envreg/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/env_help.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/env_help_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/env_registry_test.go
' covers: internal/imagebuild/targets.go (Specs: Override, ParentOverride, NeedsOverride)
'   the on/off vocabulary ............ _spec/internal/envflag/env-switches.puml
'   where `help env` is listed ........ _spec/cmd/proveo/usage.puml
'   the decision record ............... _spec/_plans/repo-simplification.puml (N8)
'   open PROVEO_* findings ............ _spec/_plans/repo-simplification.puml (N27-N33)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT IT REPLACED (N8, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ────────────────────────────
' The first read found about 85 distinct "PROVEO_*" literals in non-test Go,
' and the operator docs named eight of them. Nothing listed the rest, and
' nothing noticed when a reader went away.
'
' ── THE SHAPE (MEASURED, internal/envreg/envreg.go) ────────────────────────
'   Scope    Operator — a user sets it on the host
'            Maintainer — build, release, CI or test tooling sets it
'            Internal — proveo sets it for its own processes or the sandbox
'            String() names each for the help headings
'   Var      {Name, Scope, Default, Doc}: Default says what happens when it is
'            unset, Doc what setting it does
'   Vars     76 entries, by scope then name: Operator 29, Maintainer 26,
'            Internal 21 (reported)
'   ByScope  the Vars of one scope, in Vars order
' That is the whole exported API. The review deleted Lookup, Family, Matches
' and Scopes because no non-test code called them (MEASURED: none remain).
'
' ONE FAMILY: PROVEO_<TARGET>_IMAGE. It stands for the image override names
' internal/imagebuild declares: every Override, ParentOverride and
' NeedsOverride in imagebuild.Specs, including the ones browserOf builds at
' runtime through envName, such as PROVEO_CODEX_BROWSER_IMAGE. Its Doc says
' the claudecode* targets take no override, because their Specs rows carry
' none (MEASURED, targets.go).
'
' Doc and Default corrections from the review (MEASURED):
'   PROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION  default "ask on a TTY with the wizard on, else decline"
'   PROVEO_DEPS            the image also reads `off`
'   PROVEO_SBX_INSTANCES   divides Docker's memory total by N
'   PROVEO_PLATFORMS       only a comma-separated list is cut to the host
'                          platform on --load
' PROVEO_BIN is deleted from the registry, and build-cli no longer tells a
' maintainer to set it: nothing ever read it.
'
' ── `proveo help env` (cmd/proveo/env_help.go) ─────────────────────────────
' MEASURED: envHelpCmd has no Run, so cobra treats it as a help topic, and root
' help lists it under "help topics" (cmd/proveo/help.go renderHelp), not under
' "commands". renderEnvHelp draws an "operator" and a "maintainer" heading
' through ByScope, one row per variable: the name, then Doc and "(default …)".
' Internal rows are omitted. Reported: `proveo env` renders the same page.
' README.md "Environment variables" (reported): `proveo help env` lists every
' PROVEO_* variable the proveo binaries read. Variables only the image
' entrypoints read, such as PROVEO_BROWSER_SKILL, live in each def's README.
' The on/off spellings apply to the switches the binaries read.
' FIXED 2026-10-18 (MEASURED): README.md now says `proveo help env` lists every
' PROVEO_* variable a user or maintainer can set for the binaries, and that the
' variables proveo sets for itself (the 21 Internal rows) are left out.
'
' ── THE GUARDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' internal/contract/env_registry_test.go:
'   TestEveryProveoVariableIsRegistered
'     every override name in imagebuild.Specs must be registered by name or
'     through the family; every PROVEO_* name inside a string literal of
'     non-test Go under cmd/ and internal/ must be registered by name, or be
'     one of those override names with the family registered. So an unrelated
'     PROVEO_FOO_IMAGE literal fails instead of passing through the family.
'     MEASURED by the coordinator: red with a temporary unregistered literal,
'     then green.
'   TestEveryRegisteredVariableIsStillUsed
'     every non-family entry must still appear in such a literal.
' internal/envreg/envreg_test.go pins the table: unique names; a literal or one
' family; Doc and Default one line and non-empty (≤90 runes, reported); known
' scopes; scope-then-name order.
' cmd/proveo/env_help_test.go: TestHelpEnvListsEveryOperatorAndMaintainerVariable
' (no Internal rows) and TestProveoHelpEnvRendersTheRegistry (`help env` runs;
' root help names it).
'
' KNOWN LIMIT (review, recorded, not fixed): the literal scan sees whole string
' literals only. A name assembled with fmt.Sprintf or concatenation escapes
' it; the image overrides are covered only because the test reads Specs.
'
' ── BOUNDARY: Go UNDER cmd/ AND internal/ ONLY ─────────────────────────────
' The scan reads Go string literals. PROVEO_SKIP_INIT is read only by the
' installer scripts, and the image entrypoints read their own PROVEO_* in shell
' (reported). Neither is registered, and neither test can see them. The env
' audit filed this gap as N32 (PROPOSED: an Image scope plus a shell scan).
'
' ── OPEN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED: PROVEO_SEED_DONE_MARKER is read with a default (internal/sbx/kit.go
' startup script, packages/lib/proveo-seed), and only tests set it. It stays
' registered while a literal names it; filed as N27 (PROPOSED).
' PROVEO_DEPS has two vocabularies, one per reader: filed as N29 (PROPOSED).
' The deprecated aliases PROVEO_EGRESS_ROOT and PROVEO_EGRESS_ENV_FILE are due
' to expire: filed as N33 (PROPOSED).
' [Unverified] PROVEO_SBX_MEMORY and PROVEO_SBX_CPUS: unset, proveo omits -m and
' --cpus; sbx's own default is not measured.
' [Inference] PROVEO_DEPS reaches the image through the project .env seed; no Go
' code forwards it.
title envreg — every PROVEO_* variable proveo's Go reads or sets, and who sets it

node "internal/envreg" as REG <<host>> {
  database "Vars — 76 entries\nscope, then name" as VARS <<db>>
  component "PROVEO_<TARGET>_IMAGE\nthe one family entry" as FAM <<app>>
}

node "Scope" as SC <<host>> {
  component "operator · 29\na user, on the host" as OPS <<app>>
  component "maintainer · 26\nbuild · release · CI · tests" as MNT <<app>>
  component "internal · 21\nproveo, for itself and the sandbox" as INT <<app>>
}

component "proveo help env\nrenderEnvHelp via ByScope" as HELP <<app>>
component "PROVEO_* in string literals\nnon-test Go under cmd/ and internal/" as LIT <<app>>
component "imagebuild.Specs\nOverride · ParentOverride · NeedsOverride" as OVR <<app>>
component "TestEveryProveoVariableIsRegistered\nTestEveryRegisteredVariableIsStillUsed" as TESTS <<app>>
component "shell: installer scripts\nimage entrypoints" as SH <<error>>

VARS ARROW_MAIN SC
OPS ARROW_MAIN HELP : one row each
MNT ARROW_MAIN HELP : one row each
INT ARROW_OPTIONAL HELP : omitted
TESTS ARROW_MAIN LIT : every name registered
TESTS ARROW_MAIN OVR : every override covered
TESTS ARROW_MAIN VARS : every literal row still named
OVR ARROW_MAIN FAM : the only names it admits
SH ARROW_OPTIONAL LIT : not scanned

note right of SC
  **Scope records who sets a variable.**
  The help page lists operator and maintainer
  rows only, because internal variables carry
  values proveo computes for its own processes
  and the sandbox.
end note

note bottom of FAM
  **The family is checked against real names.**
  The registry test collects every override
  name imagebuild.Specs declares, so the family
  admits exactly those and an unrelated *_IMAGE
  literal still fails.
end note

note bottom of TESTS
  **Two tests, one per direction.** An
  unregistered literal fails the first and an
  unused registry entry fails the second, so
  documentation and implementation cannot
  diverge unnoticed.
end note

note bottom of SH
  **The scan reads Go literals only.**
  Installer scripts and image entrypoints parse
  their own PROVEO_* variables in shell, so
  neither registry test can observe or
  validate them.
end note
@enduml
